                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "In the current patchset I've suggested to print unknown formats as\n```\n<...>,\n<property name> : null,\n<...>,\n```\nIf we don't want to do that and want to use the current behaviour, i.e skip such properties completely, we need to somehow update the `bejProcessEnding` function, since currently it always produces commas. I.e. in the example above it we will produce:\n```\n<...>,\n,\n<...>,\n```\nPlease write your opinion which way should we go."
                },
