                {
                    "file": "src/bej_decoder_core.c",
                    "line": 832,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brandon Kim",
                        "email": "brandonkim@google.com",
                        "username": "brandonkimbk"
                    },
                    "message": "minor nit: could this potentially flood the logs if we have a corrupted message? maybe consider debug flag / rate limit"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/bej_decoder_core.c",
                    "line": 832,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "I think the corruption should be very specific for this to be an issue.\n\nThe code processes SFLV tuples. So to get the issue we need every L small enough to get many records. And in every message we need to have F with some unknown value.\n\nSo in this regard this case becomes no different from JSON with many BejBytestring/BejChoice/BejResourceLink records, where the current code simply prints:\n```No BejBytestring/BejChoice/BejResourceLink support```\n\nSo if we would want to introduce some debug flag / rate limit, we should probably do it general in libbej, including the print mentioned above. With this in mind I think this is a completely separate change and shouldn' be covered in this patchset"
                }
            ],
